WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.772
Let’s begin with the smallest useful function.

00:00:02.772 --> 00:00:08.302
Show_welcome takes no inputs. Its only job is to print a message.

00:00:08.302 --> 00:00:13.002
When Python reads the definition, it stores the instructions.

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:16.785
Nothing is printed until we call show_welcome at the bottom.

00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:21.491
Change the message inside the function and run the cell again.

00:00:21.491 --> 00:00:26.326
The structure stays the same even though the behavior changes.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:33.028
This example is simple, but the define-then-call pattern stays the same for more complex functions.
